---
import MarketingLayout from '../layouts/Marketing.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/layout/PageHero.astro';
import FinalCta from '../components/sections/FinalCta.astro';

const pageTitle = 'About Pagayo — One platform, every way you sell.';
const pageDescription =
  'Pagayo is a commerce platform built from one idea: a sale is a sale. Learn what we believe, how Pagayo is built, and where it is going.';
---

<MarketingLayout title={pageTitle} description={pageDescription}>
  <main class="about-page">

    <!-- Hero -->
    <PageHero label="About Pagayo">
      <Fragment slot="title">
        One platform.<br />
        <span class="text-gradient">Every way you sell.</span>
      </Fragment>
      <p class="text-lg" slot="intro">
        Pagayo is a commerce platform built on a single idea — and shaped,
        week by week, by the people who use it.
      </p>
    </PageHero>

    <!-- Manifesto echo -->
    <section class="section about-belief">
      <div class="container narrow">
        <h2 class="headline-md">A sale is a sale.</h2>
        <p>
          A subscription, a webshop checkout, a register at the counter, a
          membership renewal, a sponsored seat for someone who couldn't
          otherwise afford it — they are all the same thing. They are all
          <strong>one Order</strong>.
        </p>
        <p>
          Most platforms hide that truth behind separate products, separate
          dashboards, separate invoices, separate logins. Pagayo refuses to.
          Every sale, wherever it happens, flows into the same Order, the
          same admin, the same numbers.
        </p>
        <p>
          That single decision is what makes everything else possible: clean
          reporting, predictable pricing, no duplicate work, no surprises at
          the end of the month.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- What Pagayo is -->
    <section class="section about-what">
      <div class="container narrow">
        <span class="section-label">What Pagayo is</span>
        <h2 class="headline-md">A serious platform, accessible to everyone.</h2>
        <p>
          Pagayo bundles the tools a serious business needs — webshop, point
          of sale, subscriptions, memberships, invoicing, customer
          management, reporting — into one platform that you can use for
          free, from day one, with every feature included.
        </p>
        <p>
          You pay when you outgrow the free plan, not when you unlock a
          feature. There are no transaction fees on top, no revenue share,
          no gated modules. Your data stays yours. You can leave whenever
          you want — most operators never do.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- How it's built -->
    <section class="section about-built">
      <div class="container narrow">
        <span class="section-label">How it's built</span>
        <h2 class="headline-md">Engineered on the edge.</h2>
        <p>
          Pagayo runs on Cloudflare's global edge network. No origin
          servers, no maintenance windows, no single point of failure.
          Every page, every API call, every payment is handled close to
          your customer — wherever in the world they are.
        </p>
        <p>
          Every change goes through a pull request. Every deployment is
          automated. Every piece of infrastructure is code. We ship
          continuously because the platform is built to ship continuously
          — and because the people using Pagayo deserve a system that
          keeps getting better, every week.
        </p>
        <p class="about-link-row">
          <a href="/build-log" class="about-link">See the Build Log →</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- What we believe -->
    <section class="section about-believe">
      <div class="container narrow">
        <span class="section-label">What we believe</span>
        <h2 class="headline-md">A few quiet principles.</h2>
        <ul class="about-principles">
          <li>
            <h3>One Order, every channel.</h3>
            <p>
              The shape of the platform follows the shape of the work, not
              the other way around.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3>Free isn't a teaser.</h3>
            <p>
              The free plan is a real product. Paid plans add capacity, not
              features.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3>Boring infrastructure, exciting outcomes.</h3>
            <p>
              We choose proven, edge-native technology so you don't have to
              think about uptime, scale, or backups.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3>The roadmap is the inbox.</h3>
            <p>
              Pagayo grows from what the people using it ask for. Every
              message gets read. Every good idea finds its way in.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3>Commerce should be honest.</h3>
            <p>
              Clear pricing, clear invoices, clear data ownership. No
              dark patterns, no lock-in, no surprises.
            </p>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Where it's going -->
    <section class="section about-future">
      <div class="container narrow">
        <span class="section-label">Where it's going</span>
        <h2 class="headline-md">Built to grow with you.</h2>
        <p>
          Pagayo is still early — and that is the best part. The platform
          is being shaped right now, in public, with the people who use it.
          New modules, new channels, new integrations land continuously.
          The same Order model carries them all.
        </p>
        <p>
          If there's something you wish Pagayo did — a workflow, a report,
          a sales channel, a payment method, anything — we want to hear it.
        </p>
        <p class="about-link-row">
          <a href="/contact" class="about-link">Tell us your idea →</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <FinalCta />
  </main>
</MarketingLayout>
